.TH LOGIN 1 "September 2026" "authd" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
login \- start a Peios terminal logon session
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B login
.RB [ \-p ]
.RB [ \-H ]
.RB [ \-h
.IR host ]
.RI [ username ]
.br
.B login
.RB [ \-p ]
.RB [ \-H ]
.RB [ \-h
.IR host ]
.BR \-\-try " " username
.br
.B login
.RB [ \-p ]
.RB [ \-H ]
.RB [ \-h
.IR host ]
.BR \-\-try-no-password " " username
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B login
collects credentials through the terminal, asks the Peios authentication
authority for a primary token, installs the granted token on itself, and
replaces itself with the principal's login shell.
.PP
With no
.I username
it prompts for one.  Supplying a name selects that principal directly.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-p
Preserve the inherited environment instead of constructing a fresh login
environment.
.TP
.B \-H
Accept the conventional request to suppress a hostname banner.  The current
client emits no such banner, so this option has no further effect.
.TP
.BI \-h " host"
Record the remote peer on whose behalf this interactive logon is originated.
.TP
.BI \-\-try " username"
Attempt the named principal first and fall back to the normal prompt after a
non-fatal denial.
.TP
.BI \-\-try-no-password " username"
Attempt the named principal while advertising that the client can collect no
credentials.  If authentication requires interaction, fall back silently to
the normal prompt.
.TP
.B \-\-
End option processing.
.SH SECURITY
The traditional
.B \-f
authentication bypass is deliberately unsupported.  Authentication decisions
are made by the authority from the verified peer and cannot be asserted by a
command-line flag.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR authd (8),
.BR lps (1),
.BR lpsd (8)
